undamentally flawed because they often rely on invasive surveillance methods that disproportionately harm law-abiding citizens. Rather than protecting individual rights, these measures effectively treat the general public as potential criminals, necessitating a shift toward more effective, non-invasive strategies for reducing crime.\", \"summary\": \"Current privacy safeguards are ineffective because they rely on invasive surveillance that harms law-abiding citizens.\"}}",
